---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Content Writer"
	pubDate="Aug 17, 2026"
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
<section style="max-w: 750px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 32px; font-family: sans-serif; background-color: #ffffff; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; line-height: 1.6;">
  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px;">
    
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin: 0 0 8px 0; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">
        Crystal Morales
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: #2563eb; margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">
        B2C Content Writer & Technical Translator
      </p>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
      My specialty is simple: <strong>I take dense, confusing, or highly technical ideas and turn them into clear, enjoyable, and easy-to-read guides for everyday people.</strong> Whether someone is trying to understand software tools, creative setups, or complex step-by-step instructions, I write content that cuts through the noise so anyone can understand it on their first read.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
      Navigating the world with ADHD gives me a unique advantage as a consumer writer. Because I know firsthand how easy it is for a reader to lose focus or feel overwhelmed by a massive wall of text, I structure my writing with extreme intent. I rely heavily on clear visual hierarchies, intuitive formatting, and practical analogies. If an article is easy for a distracted mind to follow, it is going to be incredibly effective for your target customers.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
      I treat writing as a collaborative process. Rather than claiming to have every technical answer memorized, my strength lies in my curiosity, my ability to research deeply, and my skill at asking the right questions. I take complex source material—manuals, developer notes, or raw concepts—and shape it into a polished, accessible portfolio piece that casual readers actually enjoy using.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top: 8px;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: 0 0 12px 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">
        What I Bring to Your Team
      </h3>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; color: #475569; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; font-size: 15px;">
        <li><strong>Layman Translation:</strong> Converting multi-step workflows, documentation, or creative concepts into friendly, conversational blog posts.</li>
        <li><strong>Reader-First Structure:</strong> Using highly scannable layouts, clear headings, and clean tables so articles never feel intimidating.</li>
        <li><strong>SEO Basics & Clarity:</strong> Ensuring text is naturally organized so search engines find it easily, while keeping the human reader's enjoyment as the number one priority.</li>
        <li><strong>Local Code Literacy:</strong> Basic familiarity with tools like GitHub, Markdown, and static site configurations to help get content published smoothly without requiring constant developer intervention.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div style="background-color: #f8fafc; padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 4px solid #2563eb; margin-top: 12px;">
      <p style="font-size: 14px; margin: 0; color: #334155; font-weight: 500;">
        I am currently looking for a writing role where I can support a team by keeping content clear, approachable, and actionable. Feel free to explore my structured writing samples below.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
